From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: PS5: a child to be debugged starts in a helper.

NtCreateUserProcess refused a child with a debug object (DEBUG_PROCESS) with STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED, a refusal the
first experimental child loader made and nothing measured since. Wine's debug events (a new process, its threads and
modules, its exceptions) come from the server and the debuggee's own ntdll, not from ptrace, and the debuggee's
thread contexts and memory already go through the console's own paths (patch 1172, the memory service). kernel32
process test_DebuggingFlag created such a child, then waited in WaitForDebugEvent(INFINITE) for a debuggee that
never existed, and the file ended at its 900 s budget in both builds (2026-10-25); ntdll exception's debuggee tests
answered error 50 (exception.c:9809, 1295). The child now starts, with the debug object passed to the server.
---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/process.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/process.c
index 6fdc1ed..c75da08 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/process.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/process.c
@@ -868,10 +868,11 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtCreateUserProcess( HANDLE *process_handle_ptr, HANDLE *thread_
         goto done;
     }
 #ifdef __PROSPERO__
-    /* Experimental Sony service loader: PE64 and, under WoW64, PE32, explicitly enabled. */
+    /* Experimental Sony service loader: PE64 and, under WoW64, PE32, explicitly enabled. A child to be debugged
+     * starts too: Wine's debug events come from the server and the debuggee's own ntdll, not from ptrace (patch 2094). */
     if (!getenv("WINE_PS5_CHILDREN") || strcmp(getenv("WINE_PS5_CHILDREN"), "1") ||
         (getenv("WINE_PS5_CHILD") && !getenv("WINE_PS5_INITIAL_CLIENT") &&
-         !ps5_descendants_enabled( &params->ImagePathName )) || debug ||
+         !ps5_descendants_enabled( &params->ImagePathName )) ||
         !ps5_child_machine( pe_info.machine ) || (machine && !ps5_child_machine( machine )))
     {
         status = STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED;
